{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who knows</b> — Rabbi Moses said: this verse is linked to the one after it, and the meaning is: every man who knows the might of Your anger and knows to count his days truly, the truth is made known to him, and he is a prophet, for he has a heart of wisdom. And he interprets it thus like the daughters of Zelophehad, and the word הודע is like \"return my silver,\" and on this pattern: \"or make known to him his sin that he sinned.\" And in my opinion: \"Who knows\" — who is this that can comprehend the might of Your anger?! And according to the fear of You, so is Your wrath, in the manner of \"I will be sanctified through those near to Me,\" as our predecessors expounded it on the word וסביביו, \"is feared exceedingly.\""], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:50.657356661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}